[COMMENTS]
STATION,Trapezoidal critical depth flume with ultrasonic gauge. Some of the vegetation and trees on banks encroach on the river and possibly restrict flow. GENERAL: Station located approx. 2km east of Chippenham and was opened in 1970. Trapezoidal critical depth flume. Ultrasonic gauge installed 11/2007. STATION HYDROMETRY: Full range station. Level only station prior to 07/1969. Stanley Bridge, 100 - 150m upstream, causes throttling at high flows. Significant bypassing occurs at highest flows (e.g. 07/2007). One peak flow rating applied across period of record. Top end modelled and verified by ultrasonic readings. The river bed is composed of gravel and is lined with trees and vegetation, some of the vegetation and trees encroach on the river and possibly restrict flow. Water levels frequently reach the structure's capacity. Few high flow gaugings. Suffers from backing up, mainly at high flows. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8) and in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Minor surface water abstractions and discharges in catchment. Some milling takes place.
CATCHMENT,The catchment is predominantly rural with the towns of Calne and Lyneham the only significant urban areas. Geologically, the catchment is dominated by Oxford Clay and other impermeables with Chalk outcrops in headwaters. No major catchment changes.
Qmed Suitability,Good fit to available gaugings and theoretical rating expected to perform well.
Pooling Suitability,Limited gauging of floodplain flow, but confidence in modelled top end of rating that accounts for backwater and bypassing.
[END]
